  "id": "hypoxemia",
  "term": "hypoxemia",
  "definition": "Hypoxemia is a state of low oxygen in arterial blood, conventionally identified by a reduced arterial oxygen pressure on blood gas testing. In monitoring, oxygen saturation readings are often used as a real-time stand-in, but by themselves they may be misleading and need to be interpreted with other patient measures.",
